contentText:
Jurors heard closing arguments on Monday (Aug. 31) in the murder trial over the killing of Tupac Shakur , with prosecutors telling them that Duane &ldquo;Keffe D&rdquo; Davis admitted to &ldquo;hunting&rdquo; the rapper &mdash; and that his later disavowals of his story &ldquo;make no sense.&rdquo;

Wrapping up a two-week trial over the long-unsolved 1996 drive-by shooting that left the rapper dead at 25, prosecutor Binu Palal told jurors that Davis had sought revenge after Tupac beat up his nephew earlier that night at a Las Vegas casino.

